{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink bundle feels like a useful next step because it connects my earlier interest in home security with the Alexa devices I already use.",
    "The mesh Wi-Fi system addresses a plausible need as I add connected home devices, especially given my previous range extender purchase.",
    "The storage recommendations fit my history of buying drives, memory cards and readers, although I need a specific use and compatible device before choosing either."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another Fire TV stick and an older Echo Show overlap with devices I recently bought, so their familiarity does not make them useful purchases today.",
    "Earbuds and a tablet do not address a current need for me; my recent purchases give clearer reasons to consider home equipment and computer peripherals.",
    "The USB-C cables and AirTag require compatibility that my history does not establish, so I would not choose them just because I buy electronics."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to be treated as interest in any Alexa device, even when a recommendation repeats a function I recently covered.",
    "My interest in practical electronics seems to extend too broadly to gadgets without a clear connection to something I need now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Recent purchases matter because they can satisfy a need: my Fire TV Stick 4K Max and Echo Show 5 make similar devices less compelling right now.",
    "I care about how an accessory fits equipment I actually own, including its ports, storage format and installation requirements.",
    "An addition that helps my existing setup, such as home security or better Wi-Fi coverage, feels more useful than another device with overlapping functions."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in practical home electronics but sometimes confuse familiar products with useful next purchases."
}"}
